### 2. .gitignore
This is a "hidden" file that tells GitHub to ignore the files that only your computer needs. This keeps your repository clean. Create a file named `.gitignore` (make sure the dot is at the front) and paste this:

```text
# Ignore Executables
*.exe
*.out
*.app

# Ignore Build Objects
*.o
*.obj

# Debugging symbols
*.pdb
*.dSYM/

# IDE specific folders (VS Code / Visual Studio)
.vscode/
.vs/
out/
bin/
